MODULE visualization_tools.plot_graph
STATUS non-executable diagnostic plotting specification.
PAPER_MAP: Section 5.2 convergence diagnostics; Sections 5.3 and 5.6; metric Equations (34)-(37).
INPUT Numerical source data, checkpoint identity and metric definitions accompany each plot.
GLOBAL INPUT CONTRACT:
    Epoch history records carry actual epoch labels and formula-index metadata.
    Batch history records carry epoch, batch, and global_optimizer_step separately.
    Utility history distinguishes optimizer-step samples from end-of-epoch samples.
    OD tensors use [sample,horizon,origin,compressed_destination_slot].
    Compressed slots map through fixed RDS[origin,slot].
    The last slot is the residual aggregate and is never mislabeled as one destination station.
    Prediction bundles contain checkpoint_id, split, sample_ids, target_times, and masks.
    Truth bundles contain the same ordered identifiers and target-time semantics.
    Values are original passenger-flow counts unless a stored transform is explicitly supplied.
    Metrics carry their definition, reduction order, and ratio-versus-percent unit.
    The plotter cannot recover any of these contracts from array length alone.
GLOBAL OUTPUT CONTRACT:
    Figure artifact in the requested export format.
    Sidecar metadata naming source artifacts, units, selections, and checkpoint identity.
    Export receipt with destination and validation status.
    File outputs belong to the supplied diagnostic directory, never a source workbook-as-directory.
    No plot is labeled an independently reproduced paper result without separate evidence.

PROCEDURE plot_step_points_from_excel
    INPUT filepath, columns, step, output_pdf.
    PARAMETERS sheet_name, index_column, index_kind, column_units, export_options.
    OUTPUT utility-trajectory figure and source-index metadata.
    READ the selected workbook sheet as a tabular data source.
    REQUIRE every requested column exists.
    REQUIRE index_column exists and is numeric or otherwise a declared ordered axis.
    REQUIRE index_kind is epoch or global_optimizer_step.
    IF the source is a per-batch utility table:
        USE global_optimizer_step for its primary x coordinate.
        KEEP epoch and batch as annotations or sidecar metadata.
    ELSE IF the source contains one selected value per epoch:
        USE its stored actual epoch numbers.
        VERIFY only one value exists for each displayed epoch.
    END IF
    SORT rows by the declared x coordinate.
    CHECK duplicate x values against the declared trajectory sampling convention.
    PRESERVE gaps from missing measurements.
    REQUIRE step is a positive marker-selection cadence.
    DECLARE whether step counts observations or x-axis units.
    SELECT marker positions accordingly, without altering the underlying trajectory.
    RETAIN the first and final valid measurement when the export policy requests endpoints.
    CREATE one labeled curve per requested utility coefficient.
    LABEL the station coefficient with its station-count feature convention.
    LABEL the transfer coefficient with its transfer-count feature convention.
    IF coefficients have incomparable units:
        USE separate aligned panels rather than an unexplained common scale.
    END IF
    ADD a legend identifying each coefficient and any initial prior reference.
    LABEL x as the actual index_kind and y as the corresponding utility coefficient.
    INCLUDE the run/checkpoint or trajectory identity in metadata.
    RESOLVE output_pdf under the requested diagnostic directory.
    IF filepath names an .xlsx file:
        Resolve the PDF inside the supplied diagnostic output directory.
    END IF
    RENDER and export using the declared page size, font, and resolution settings.
    VERIFY output exists, is nonempty, and has readable axes and legends.
    RETURN figure receipt and plotted source rows.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE plot_metric_pair
    INPUT x_epochs, train_values, validation_values, metric_name, save_dir.
    PARAMETERS separate_epoch_indices, metric_definition, units, masks, export_options.
    OUTPUT paired training/validation metric figure.
    REQUIRE explicit actual epoch coordinates for each series.
    CHECK each series length against its own coordinate list.
    ACCEPT a common x_epochs list only when both series truly share it.
    PRESERVE unevaluated training or validation epochs as missing, not zeros.
    VERIFY both series represent the same mathematical metric and reduction order.
    IF train_values are the weighted optimization objective and validation_values are MAE:
        REJECT a single generically labeled Loss comparison.
        REQUIRE separate panels or separately named quantities.
    END IF
    IF metric metadata identifies WMAPE as a ratio:
        MULTIPLY by 100 only for a percent-labeled display.
        RECORD the conversion in the sidecar.
    ELSE IF values are already percentages:
        Use the supplied percentage values unchanged.
    END IF
    LABEL MAE and RMSE in passenger-flow units.
    LABEL WMAPE or SMAPE with the appropriate percentage definition.
    PLOT training and validation as distinct styles with a legible legend.
    MARK selected-checkpoint epoch only when selection metadata supplies it.
    Use the sealed selection_metadata when marking the selected epoch.
    KEEP all evaluated epochs at their actual coordinates.
    DISPLAY undefined metric values as gaps with an explained denominator status.
    EXPORT under a sanitized metric-specific filename in save_dir.
    WRITE source metric schema, units, reduction, and epoch lists beside the figure.
    RETURN validated export receipt.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE plot_training_curves
    INPUT train_losses, val_mae_list, val_mape_list, val_rmse_list, save_dir.
    PARAMETERS epoch_history, loss_kind, metric_metadata, selection_metadata, export_options.
    OUTPUT convergence panels with distinct labeled quantities.
    REQUIRE epoch coordinates for every supplied curve.
    PREFER the structured epoch_history exported by the training procedure.
    ADAPT legacy arrays only when their coordinate and unit metadata are supplied.
    IDENTIFY whether train_losses means OD MAE, total objective, or generation penalty.
    FOR the principal OD convergence panel:
        USE original-scale training OD MAE.
        USE validation MAE under the declared inference/evaluation protocol.
        LABEL any training teacher-forcing versus validation autoregressive difference.
    END FOR
    PLACE validation RMSE in a separately labeled panel or explicitly compatible axis.
    PLACE validation WMAPE in a percentage panel.
    IF the legacy val_mape_list actually stores WMAPE:
        USE the WMAPE label and its recorded ratio/percentage conversion.
    END IF
    IF total optimization objective is also requested:
        CREATE a separate diagnostic panel.
        SHOW its exact loss name and generation-weight schedule.
    END IF
    IF generation squared-error sum is requested:
        LABEL its aggregation and squared-flow units separately.
    END IF
    KEEP training and validation legends consistent across panels.
    MARK missing measurements without interpolating them into reported results.
    SHOW early stopping or selected checkpoint only from saved run metadata.
    LABEL post-hoc test curves separately if they are explicitly supplied.
    SUPPORT the legacy no_pinn_loss directory name only as an OD-only-loss export alias.
    EXPORT figures and a table of plotted values with their actual epoch indices.
    VERIFY labels distinguish all metrics and scales.
    RETURN export receipts and the plotted history subset.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE plot_od_losses
    INPUT epoch_od_errors_list, selected_pairs, save_path.
    PARAMETERS evaluated_epochs, RDS, station_names, error_definition, selection_metadata.
    OUTPUT per-OD error trajectories.
    REQUIRE error tensors use [evaluated_epoch,N,K] or a declared horizon-resolved extension.
    REQUIRE evaluated_epochs matches the number and ordering of error records.
    VALIDATE each selected record contains origin, retained_slot, and real destination identity.
    CHECK destination equals RDS[origin,retained_slot].
    IF residual diagnostics are requested:
        LABEL the slot as Other destinations / residual aggregate.
    END IF
    REQUIRE selected_pairs came directly from the scored valid-pair list.
    IF only indices into a filtered candidate list are supplied:
        REQUIRE that exact filtered list.
    END IF
    FOR EACH selected pair:
        SELECT its matching tensor coordinate at every evaluated epoch.
        PRESERVE missing values or zero-denominator errors explicitly.
        IF errors are horizon-resolved:
            PLOT separate horizons or apply the declared reported reduction.
            RECORD which choice was made.
        END IF
        LABEL the curve with origin and actual destination station identifiers.
    END FOR
    LABEL x with actual evaluated epochs.
    LABEL y with the supplied error metric and original-scale unit.
    ATTACH the pair-selection rule and selection split to metadata.
    IF pairs were selected by relative improvement:
        PRESERVE signed improvement scores in the accompanying table.
    ELSE IF selected by absolute change magnitude:
        LABEL that quantity as change magnitude, not improvement.
    END IF
    STATE that selected OD illustrations are post-hoc examples, not all-OD averages.
    EXPORT the figure and selected-pair identity table.
    VERIFY no pair label or compressed index has changed during plotting.
    RETURN export receipt.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE plot_od_time_series
    INPUT y_true_all, y_pred_all, selected_pairs, save_dir.
    PARAMETERS prediction_manifest, truth_manifest, RDS, units, horizon_policy, export_options.
    OUTPUT matched truth/prediction time-series panels for selected real OD pairs.
    REQUIRE one declared selected-checkpoint prediction bundle.
    REQUIRE prediction tensor shape [B,L_f,N,K].
    REQUIRE truth tensor and observation masks use matching axes.
    JOIN truth and predictions by sample_id rather than truncating both to the shorter length.
    CHECK every joined sample's forecast origin and target timestamp array.
    REJECT missing, duplicate, or mismatched samples unless an explicit subset is requested.
    EXCLUDE padded batch rows using the genuine-sample validity mask.
    VERIFY the prediction artifact comes from the selected checkpoint and correct split.
    INVERT the stored OD transform exactly once if values are normalized.
    CHECK original-scale status before applying any inverse transform.
    RETAIN valid negative predictions as model outputs if the model allowed them.
    Plot the prediction array under its recorded output policy.
    VERIFY each selected pair's origin/slot/destination identity against RDS.
    FOR EACH selected pair:
        FOR EACH requested forecast horizon lambda:
            EXTRACT truth and prediction at that exact horizon and pair coordinate.
            EXTRACT the matching target timestamps and forecast origins.
            SORT within the series by target timestamp, retaining forecast-origin provenance.
            BREAK line segments across missing timestamps or missing observations.
            PLOT observed and predicted demand as distinct labeled styles.
            LABEL the horizon as lambda intervals and its duration in declared time units.
        END FOR
        DEFAULT representation uses separate horizon panels or distinguishable horizon curves.
        IF multiple horizons predict the same target timestamp:
            KEEP them distinct by (forecast_origin,horizon,target_time).
        END IF
        IF the caller requests one merged trajectory:
            REQUIRE an explicit horizon-selection or combination rule.
            APPLY the same stated rule consistently to every target timestamp.
            LABEL the output as a derived diagnostic, not raw model forecasts.
            VERIFY repeated truth values agree before deduplicating observations.
        END IF
        LABEL y as passengers per declared entry interval in the original flow scale.
        LABEL x with timezone-aware target time and service date when needed.
        LABEL the OD pair using canonical station names.
        ADD truth/prediction and horizon legends.
        EXPORT a pair-specific figure and the exact plotted row table.
    END FOR
    RECORD checkpoint ID, split, sample subset, horizon policy, and transformation ID.
    RETURN all figure receipts and plotted-data references.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE plot_od_time_series_first_step
    INPUT y_true_all, y_pred_all, selected_pairs, save_dir.
    PARAMETERS prediction_manifest, truth_manifest, RDS, units, export_options.
    OUTPUT first-horizon OD time-series figures.
    REQUIRE L_f is at least one.
    VERIFY the first stored horizon corresponds to lambda=1 at target time t0.
    SELECT horizon index zero in zero-based storage, retaining a length-one horizon axis.
    SELECT the identical target timestamps, masks, and metadata slice.
    CALL plot_od_time_series with an explicit first-horizon-only policy.
    USE a distinct filename suffix so multi-horizon plots are not overwritten.
    LABEL horizon as one interval, not one minute unless the interval actually is one minute.
    IF repeated forecast origins occur:
        APPLY the declared duplicate-sample policy before plotting.
    END IF
    RETAIN selected-checkpoint and original-scale checks from the shared procedure.
    RETURN first-step export receipts.
END PROCEDURE

MODULE_FLOW:
    The training exporter calls these procedures only after its numerical artifacts are sealed.
    All requested formats, font choices, canvas sizes, and DPI values are caller-supplied decisions.
    Export validation checks nonempty files, complete legends, unclipped labels, and correct units.
    Plotting errors are reported as diagnostic-export failures rather than model-training successes.
    This specification creates no figure files by itself and changes no project website content.
